{"duration_api_ms":122564,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"d3e34e05-3032-4d00-aa89-0d420bfc98d7","total_cost_usd":0.35678719999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26391,"cache_read_input_tokens":720326,"output_tokens":10709,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3977},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26391,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1741,"cache_read_input_tokens":50055,"cache_creation_input_tokens":667,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":667},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":34,"outputTokens":10709,"cacheReadInputTokens":720326,"cacheCreationInputTokens":26391,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.35678719999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3977,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":18,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Deployed and verified an \\\"inventory application\\\" on node1 (RHEL 7.9) served over TCP 8181 with SELinux in enforcing mode throughout, then completed the mandatory single-node restart/recovery protocol.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed node1: RHEL 7.9, SELinux enforcing (SELINUXTYPE=targeted), no repos/subscription so no package installs possible (semanage/semodule/checkmodule/audit2allow all absent), no pre-existing inventory app.\",\"Created /opt/inventory-app/index.html (inventory listing) and /opt/inventory-app/server.py (Python2 BaseHTTPServer/SimpleHTTPServer) bound to 0.0.0.0:8181; applied SELinux file contexts (bin_t on server.py, httpd_sys_content_t on index.html).\",\"Created and enabled systemd unit inventory-app.service (ExecStart=/usr/bin/python2 /opt/inventory-app/server.py, Restart=on-failure, WantedBy=multi-user.target); started it via systemctl.\",\"Opened TCP 8181 permanently in firewalld and reloaded.\",\"Verified service runs in system_u:system_r:unconfined_service_t domain, listens on *:8181, and HTTP 200 responses returned via both 127.0.0.1 and $NODE_IP while `getenforce` reported Enforcing at every check; confirmed no AVC denials (dmesg/audit log empty/absent).\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and service/SELinux baseline, issued a detached `sudo -n reboot` on node1, polled node1 until exec connectivity returned, confirmed boot_id changed (809708f3... -> 9ea46e0a...), and re-verified SELinux enforcing, service active+enabled, port listening, firewalld rule persisted, and HTTP 200 after reboot.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: SELinux enforcing and system state before changes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-27d5d51c238344fb\",\"cmd-703cfed896984d3c\",\"cmd-f6cc139f87974f40\",\"cmd-7402e601b74e4d2f\",\"cmd-91e5b62207604c41\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed RHEL 7.9, SELINUX=enforcing, no package manager access, and absence of semanage/semodule tooling, establishing the constraint that the app must run in a domain compatible with enforcing SELinux without new port policy modules.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Inventory application served on TCP 8181 while SELinux stays enforcing\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4ebb20e22d3b41e9\"],\"summary\":\"Deployed inventory-app.service, confirmed getenforce=Enforcing before and after start, service active, listening on *:8181 as unconfined_service_t, firewalld port 8181/tcp opened, and curl to 127.0.0.1:8181 and $NODE_IP:8181 both returned HTTP 200 with inventory content; no AVC denials found.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline capture\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-be2c291953d24d95\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 809708f3-1c5f-4e37-ad6a-8bcbae408799, service enabled state, and Enforcing SELinux status prior to restarting node1.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement and node unavailability\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5504f20b0bac4ad0\",\"cmd-ffe8414e4b7c4698\",\"cmd-42a0143d44bf4349\"],\"summary\":\"Issued a detached sudo -n reboot that returned its acknowledgement before disconnecting; subsequent exec attempts timed out, confirming the node was mid-restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proving the restart occurred\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7152ae35d3ee409b\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id read back as 9ea46e0a-ee13-4d39-806a-25b40765c05f, differing from the pre-restart 809708f3-... value, proving a genuine reboot rather than mere service restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required services, data, and SELinux enforcement\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7171630fbecd4337\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, getenforce still Enforcing, inventory-app.service active and enabled, listening on 8181 in unconfined_service_t, firewalld still has 8181/tcp open, and curl to $NODE_IP:8181 returned HTTP 200 with the inventory page.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed and verified an \"inventory application\" on node1 (RHEL 7.9) served over TCP 8181 with SELinux in enforcing mode throughout, then completed the mandatory single-node restart/recovery protocol.","actions_performed":["Surveyed node1: RHEL 7.9, SELinux enforcing (SELINUXTYPE=targeted), no repos/subscription so no package installs possible (semanage/semodule/checkmodule/audit2allow all absent), no pre-existing inventory app.","Created /opt/inventory-app/index.html (inventory listing) and /opt/inventory-app/server.py (Python2 BaseHTTPServer/SimpleHTTPServer) bound to 0.0.0.0:8181; applied SELinux file contexts (bin_t on server.py, httpd_sys_content_t on index.html).","Created and enabled systemd unit inventory-app.service (ExecStart=/usr/bin/python2 /opt/inventory-app/server.py, Restart=on-failure, WantedBy=multi-user.target); started it via systemctl.","Opened TCP 8181 permanently in firewalld and reloaded.","Verified service runs in system_u:system_r:unconfined_service_t domain, listens on *:8181, and HTTP 200 responses returned via both 127.0.0.1 and $NODE_IP while `getenforce` reported Enforcing at every check; confirmed no AVC denials (dmesg/audit log empty/absent).","Captured pre-restart boot_id and service/SELinux baseline, issued a detached `sudo -n reboot` on node1, polled node1 until exec connectivity returned, confirmed boot_id changed (809708f3... -> 9ea46e0a...), and re-verified SELinux enforcing, service active+enabled, port listening, firewalld rule persisted, and HTTP 200 after reboot."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline: SELinux enforcing and system state before changes","command_ids":["cmd-27d5d51c238344fb","cmd-703cfed896984d3c","cmd-f6cc139f87974f40","cmd-7402e601b74e4d2f","cmd-91e5b62207604c41"],"summary":"Confirmed RHEL 7.9, SELINUX=enforcing, no package manager access, and absence of semanage/semodule tooling, establishing the constraint that the app must run in a domain compatible with enforcing SELinux without new port policy modules."},{"requirement":"Inventory application served on TCP 8181 while SELinux stays enforcing","command_ids":["cmd-4ebb20e22d3b41e9"],"summary":"Deployed inventory-app.service, confirmed getenforce=Enforcing before and after start, service active, listening on *:8181 as unconfined_service_t, firewalld port 8181/tcp opened, and curl to 127.0.0.1:8181 and $NODE_IP:8181 both returned HTTP 200 with inventory content; no AVC denials found."},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline capture","command_ids":["cmd-be2c291953d24d95"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 809708f3-1c5f-4e37-ad6a-8bcbae408799, service enabled state, and Enforcing SELinux status prior to restarting node1."},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement and node unavailability","command_ids":["cmd-5504f20b0bac4ad0","cmd-ffe8414e4b7c4698","cmd-42a0143d44bf4349"],"summary":"Issued a detached sudo -n reboot that returned its acknowledgement before disconnecting; subsequent exec attempts timed out, confirming the node was mid-restart."},{"requirement":"Changed boot identity proving the restart occurred","command_ids":["cmd-7152ae35d3ee409b"],"summary":"boot_id read back as 9ea46e0a-ee13-4d39-806a-25b40765c05f, differing from the pre-restart 809708f3-... value, proving a genuine reboot rather than mere service restart."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of required services, data, and SELinux enforcement","command_ids":["cmd-7171630fbecd4337"],"summary":"After reboot, getenforce still Enforcing, inventory-app.service active and enabled, listening on 8181 in unconfined_service_t, firewalld still has 8181/tcp open, and curl to $NODE_IP:8181 returned HTTP 200 with the inventory page."}]},"ttft_ms":2072,"type":"result","duration_ms":199472,"uuid":"e67ff5ae-47c0-42f4-8aba-29d6295e66f5","ttft_stream_ms":1853,"time_to_request_ms":66,"first_content_frame_ms":1853,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
